From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:29:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Turn on the SATA Power Optimizer

SataPwrOptEnable is off by default in the Coffee Lake FSP-S and the
board never set satapwroptimize. On Skylake coreboot always turns it
on, as FSP skips some SATA init registers without it.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x. Package C-states of the M920x after it, in
the hardware test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
index 59efe115a1..7ec4aa6905 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
@@ -8,6 +8,9 @@ chip soc/intel/cannonlake
 	# Enhanced Intel SpeedStep, as the OEM firmware: P-states for the OS
 	register "eist_enable" = "true"
 
+	# SATA Power Optimizer, off by default in FSP-S
+	register "satapwroptimize" = "true"
+
 	# Wake on LAN from S4 and S5, as the OEM firmware (the "wake_on_lan" option)
 	register "WolEnableOverride" = "true"
 
-- 
2.47.3

